9

This file is used to set the logging level of communications to the machine controller.

Only the first line of this file is significant, the remaining lines are documentation only.

Only the value in the first position of the first line is evaluated.


If the value = 0, or if the value is non-numeric, or if this file does not exist, only critical failures will be logged. 

If the value = 2, everything documented to be logged for lower levels will still be logged, plus,
                  all warnings and performance related log events.

If the value = 5, everything documented to be logged for lower levels will still be logged, plus,
                  every call to an externally exposed function will be logged, but just the call and the parameters sent.

If the value = 8, everything documented to be logged for lower levels will still be logged, plus,
                  detailed logging of program flow and results will be logged.

If the value = 9, everything documented to be logged for lower levels will still be logged, plus,
                  extremely detailed logging of all data flow will be logged (reserved for internal use).

Any other numeric value you provide, that is not described above, will default to the next lowest value that is described.

A value of 2 in the first position of the first line of this file is recommended unless there are other requirements.